<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-halule"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Halule</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 691 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Halule was fought in 691 BCE on the Tigris in Mesopotamia between the Neo-Assyrian Empire under Sennacherib and an alliance of Babylonians and Elamites…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hysiae"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Hysiae</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 669 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Hysiae was fought between Argos and Sparta near Hysiae in the Argolid, traditionally dated by the geographer Pausanias to 669 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ulai"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-ulai.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Ulai</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 653 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Ulai, also called the Battle of Til-Tuba, was fought around 653 BCE on the Ulai river in Elam between the army of the Assyrian king Ashurbanipal and…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hanyuan"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Hanyuan</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 645 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Hanyuan, or Battle of Han, was fought in 645 BCE between the Chinese states of Qin and Jin.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hong"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Hong</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 638 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Hong was fought in 638 BCE on the Hong River in Henan between the State of Song and the State of Chu.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chengpu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-chengpu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Chengpu</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 632 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Chengpu was fought in 632 BCE in modern Shandong between the State of Jin, under Duke Wen, with its allies Qi and Qin, and the forces of Chu and its allies.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-carchemish"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-carchemish.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Carchemish</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 605 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Carchemish was fought in 605 BCE at Carchemish on the Euphrates.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Sieges <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sennacheribs-destruction-of-babylon"><span class="enc-name">Sennacherib's destruction of Babylon</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 689 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">Sennacherib's destruction of Babylon took place in 689 BCE, when the Assyrian king captured the city after repeated rebellions and had it devastated.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/destruction-of-susa"><span class="enc-name">Destruction of Susa</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · c. 647 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The destruction of Susa was the sack of the Elamite capital by the Assyrian king Ashurbanipal around 647 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-destruction-of-susa"><span class="enc-name">Assyrian destruction of Susa</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 646 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Assyrian destruction of Susa was the sack of the Elamite capital by the army of Ashurbanipal in 646 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sack-of-assur"><span class="enc-name">Sack of Assur</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 614 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The sack of Assur was the capture of the ancient Assyrian religious capital by the Medes in 614 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/fall-of-nineveh"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fall-of-nineveh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Fall of Nineveh</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 612 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The fall of Nineveh was the destruction of the Assyrian capital in 612 BCE by a coalition of Medes and Babylonians.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/fall-of-harran"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fall-of-harran.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Fall of Harran</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 609 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The fall of Harran in 609 BCE was the defeat of the last Assyrian remnant, under Ashur-uballit II, by the Babylonians and their allies.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Wars &amp; campaigns <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-conquest-of-egypt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/assyrian-conquest-of-egypt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Assyrian conquest of Egypt</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 671 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Assyrian conquest of Egypt was the invasion of Egypt by the Assyrian king Esarhaddon, who captured Memphis in 671 BCE and drove out the Kushite pharaoh Taharqa.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/medo-babylonian-conquest-of-the-assyrian-empire"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/medo-babylonian-conquest-of-the-assyrian-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Medo-Babylonian conquest of the Assyrian Empire</span><span class="enc-type">War · 626–609 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Medo-Babylonian conquest of the Assyrian Empire was the war of 626–609 BCE in which Babylonia under Nabopolassar, joined from 615 BCE by the Medes under Cyaxares…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-invasion-of-egypt-601-bce"><span class="enc-name">Babylonian invasion of Egypt (601 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 601 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Babylonian invasion of Egypt in 601 BCE was an attempt by Nebuchadnezzar II of the Chaldean Empire to invade Egypt.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Treaties <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/covenant-of-shaoling"><span class="enc-name">Covenant of Shaoling</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 656 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Covenant of Shaoling was the agreement of 656 BCE that ended Duke Huan of Qi's campaign against the State of Chu.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/covenant-of-kuiqiu"><span class="enc-name">Covenant of Kuiqiu</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · 651 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Covenant of Kuiqiu was an assembly of Chinese feudal lords convened by Duke Huan of Qi in 651 BCE at Kuiqiu, in present-day Henan.</span></a></li></ul></section>
